      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_d0d667b6",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: jew_mad_get_fuhrererious; hasOverallIntent: hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a historical scene of Nazi Germany with Adolf Hitler and other Nazi officials in a parade, overlaid with the text 'jew mad?' and 'get fuhrererious!'. The meme uses the visual of Nazi imagery to mock or provoke a reaction, implying that Jews are 'mad' or irrational, and then sarcastically suggests they should 'get fuhrererious' (a play on 'get furious' and 'Fuhrer'), which is a direct reference to Hitler. This is a hateful meme that uses anti-Semitic tropes and Nazi imagery to demean and dehumanize Jewish people, invoking historical atrocities and promoting hate. The juxtaposition of the text with the image is designed to provoke, mock, and spread anti-Semitic sentiment, making it a clear example of hateful content targeting a protected group based on ethnicity and religion.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_4bb05e1a"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
