      "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
      "instance_name": "mapping_jew_mad_adolf_hitler",
      "label": "Jew mad? is mapped onto Adolf Hitler",
      "description": "The text 'jew mad?' is an antisemitic stereotype that implies Jewish people are irrational or hysterical. This text is juxtaposed with the visual of Adolf Hitler, who is the central figure in the Nazi parade. The mapping suggests that Hitler is the embodiment of the 'mad' Jew stereotype, or that the meme is sarcastically implying that Hitler himself is 'mad' (a reversal of the antisemitic trope). This is a hateful analogical mapping that uses Hitler's image to reinforce the dehumanizing stereotype.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
